{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor made a serious medication-safety commission by directing immediate replacement of a missed doxazosin dose based only on a home blood-pressure range, after which the patient took it. The doctor also omitted ordered coagulation/hepatitis laboratory items from the required tracking inventory and never performed the required urinary/infection symptom screen. Unsupported reassurance that a partially read CT was benign and would not affect surgery further violated bounded interpretation; any one of these serious responsibility-chain errors mandates grade 1 despite the ultimately executable discharge closure.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00719",
        "explanation": "The doctor provided a discharge medication boundary, pathology follow-up owner, and emergency escalation instructions.",
        "quote": "多沙唑嗪标注‘暂不吃’，说明目前不需要自行恢复服用"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00733",
        "explanation": "The caregiver demonstrated receipt of the medication and pathology-tracking plan.",
        "quote": "多沙唑嗪回家先不吃，不是我想恢复就恢复"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "At termination, the caregiver had an actionable discharge plan: follow the written medication list, do not independently restart doxazosin, track pathology through urology, and use emergency care for specified deterioration. This final bounded closure was executable and traceable, although it does not erase serious earlier safety errors.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
